Generic single-database configuration for Neon PostgreSQL.

Run from apps/backend:
  alembic upgrade head

Set DATABASE_URL in .env (from Neon dashboard). URL is read via get_postgres_url();
ensure it uses postgresql+asyncpg:// for async (env.py normalizes postgresql:// to that).

If the DB host is unreachable from your machine (e.g. DNS/network), create the schema
in Neon's SQL Editor instead:
  alembic upgrade head --sql > initial_schema.sql
Then paste the contents of initial_schema.sql into Neon Dashboard → SQL Editor → Run.
